Package: BBMF
Type: Package
Title: A General Nested Family of Bayesian Boolean Matrix Factorizations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(
      given = "Adolphus",
      family = "Wagala",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "adolphus@ds.dfci.harvard.edu"
    )
Description:
    Implements a general nested family of Bayesian Boolean matrix factorization
    models for binary data. The package provides five progressively restricted
    models: BBMF-Full, BBMF-NoPhi, BBMF-Flat, BBMF-Global, and BBMF-Sym.
    Functionality includes posterior inference using Markov chain Monte Carlo,
    Boolean reconstruction, MAP estimation, latent-factor recovery assessment
    using AFAS, reconstruction metrics, convergence diagnostics, and simulation
    utilities. The methodology is motivated by copy number analysis in cancer
    but is applicable to binary matrix data more generally.
